I'm rethinking the resolving strategy for FormNode.

I think FormCursor should have a "rd" property which has the ReadContext associated with it.

I think there should be a real FormTree interface:

interface FormTree {
    rootNode: FormNode;
    // Can use the read context from the ParentCursor
    createChildCursors(refId: string, parent: FormCursor): FormCursor[]; 
}

interface FormTreeResolver {
    getFormTree(formId: string): FormTree | undefined;
}

The createChildCursors method for static FormTree's is fairly straight forward as you can generate a map of id's on creation.

However the reactive FormTree will be more complicated. I think it should contain a property:

controlIdMap: Control<Record<string, Control<ControlDefinition> | undefined>

which is reactively kept up to date with any ControlDefinition which have an id field - so the tree will need a ControlContext passed in to the constructor.

